                <pb facs="0270" n="170" xml:id="pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/24168: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-07T15:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1920—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 5—1:32 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>277. My Chilean and Japanese colleagues have informed me that they are in receipt
                    of telegraphic instructions to proceed in harmony with this Embassy in regard to
                    the situation here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
